# Example only - NOT a real keystore config. Do not put real passwords in this
# file, and never commit "keystore.properties" itself (it is git-ignored).
#
# This file documents the four values app/build.gradle's signingConfigs
# .releaseConfig reads as Gradle project properties (see app/build.gradle):
#   releaseStoreFile, releaseStorePassword, releaseKeyAlias, releaseKeyPassword
#
# Local signed builds:
#   Gradle project properties are not read from a *.properties file named
#   like this automatically. Either pass them on the command line, e.g.
#     ./gradlew assembleFreeRelease \
#       -PreleaseStoreFile=/path/to/your.keystore \
#       -PreleaseStorePassword=yourStorePassword \
#       -PreleaseKeyAlias=yourKeyAlias \
#       -PreleaseKeyPassword=yourKeyPassword
#   or copy the four lines below (without the leading "# ") into your USER-level
#   ~/.gradle/gradle.properties, which lives outside this repository.
#   Do NOT put them in this repo's own gradle.properties: despite being listed
#   in .gitignore, that file is tracked upstream (git tracks it regardless of
#   the ignore rule), so passwords written there show up in `git status` and are
#   one careless `git commit -a` away from being published.
#
# releaseStoreFile=/absolute/path/to/your.keystore
# releaseStorePassword=changeit
# releaseKeyAlias=changeit
# releaseKeyPassword=changeit
#
# CI builds (.github/workflows/build-release.yml):
#   The same four values are supplied from repository secrets instead
#   (KEYSTORE_BASE64, KEYSTORE_PASSWORD, KEY_ALIAS, KEY_PASSWORD) - configure
#   those under this repo's Settings -> Secrets and variables -> Actions.
#   No real keystore or password is or should ever be committed to this repo.
